Z||000023||sameul||05-01-2001||04:59 PM||||I've been to just about every major city and boston wins hands down.  They have tiny streets that were originally made for carriges and everyone double parks because there is no space.  Its the only city i've seen where the oncoming traffic lane is considered a passing lane EVEN WITH oncoming traffic on it!  My friend pulled that maneuver and made my little heart go pitter pat(and I've gotten a speeding ticket for going 110)!||||reg||1
Z||000024||sameul||05-01-2001||05:06 PM||||Oh and the state of Florida gets my vote for worst drivers (although there are many middle states i've never been through).  Between recent immigrants who can read the signs and old people who can't remember where they put the gas pedal it a pretty dangerous place(of course old driveaway OJ Simpson lives there now, he drives a black bronco now tho).  They actually have MINIMUM SPEED LIMIT signs posted on the freeways.  I thought it was a joke when i first saw one.||||reg||1
Z||000025||DJRice||05-01-2001||07:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by johnt671:<BR><B>...Went there on my honeymoon a few years in a 78 Olds Delta 88 and got stuck on a traffic cirle for 7 laps...   </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>My first car was a Gold '78 Olds Delta 88!<P>Anyway, I actually knew a guy that got a ticket for driving too slow.  But I was down in West Palm Beach about 2 months ago and the drivers there were starting to get really flakey, but not as bad as the attractions area in Orlando.  Last summer, three Brits were killed because they were not use to the American roads and looked the wrong way before pulling out into an intersection.  I think one could use the roads in and out of the airport as an F-1 track with a few well placed barriers.  It would be one helluva track too.  First one to the Hilton wins!!!<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
