Z||000029||Spektyr||05-04-2001||05:25 AM||||In my experience I'd have to say Florida.  I lived in Orlando for awhile... never seen so many bumperstickers that say "Why do they call it Tourist Season if we can't shoot them?"<P>After a few months I started to agree.  I learned to drive in Kansas where the other motorists are basically sheep.  They'll just follow behind you until they need to turn or until you do.  In Florida you have to drive like your car is a weapon.  It's a deterrant.  If you don't seem ready to use your car to kill someone, they'll use theirs to kill you.<P>Of course Dallas' big circle-highway (can't remember the name) is certainly an interesting trip...  sure you can merge... did you bring a gun?||||reg||1
